  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Core Architecture**\n\nI\'m now structuring the frontend and core engines to establish a modular system. I\'m focusing on a clean design, starting with `/src/types.ts` to define core models and interfaces for Templates, Variables, Clauses, Rules, HealthCheck, Forms, Audit Log, Documents and the like. Next, I\'ll flesh out `/src/core/domain`, as I focus on the internal building blocks of the core engine.\n\n\n**Expanding Core Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into crucial core features. I\'m actively developing validators for Dominican identification numbers, including the Luhn algorithm for JCE C\303\251dula. Additionally, I\'m working on variable and clause engines to handle complex logic, and a rule engine for conditional evaluation. I\'m also implementing a document detector and parser, including DOCX and PDF handling.\n\n\n**Developing Core Modules**\n\nI\'ve been concentrating on error checking, focusing on identifying orphan variables, broken rules, and circular dependencies to ensure data integrity. I\'m also adding sample Dominican legal templates and a reusable clause library to `/src/core/sampleData.ts`, which I\'ll use to develop a rich structured legal document editor. I\'m actively using Zustand for a central store at `/src/store/useAppStore.ts` to manage template data and document generations. In the frontend, I\'m building UI components like a template manager and document editor, all to manage complex templates.\n\n\n**Designing Core Components**\n\nI\'m now deep in frontend design, working on an editor with a toolbar, legal numbering, and typography. I\'m also focusing on key panels: a HITL review panel for variable detection, a centralized variable manager with a tree view, and a clause library. I\'m also implementing a rule builder, a dynamic form generator with Dominican validators, and health check and version audit modals.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 73881079
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
