  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Core State**\n\nI\'m currently focused on constructing the central application store, specifically `/src/store/useAppStore.ts`. I\'ve begun identifying the required state variables, including `templates` (an array of `LegalTemplate` objects), `activeTemplateId` (a string or null), and `currentView` (a string determining the active user view).\n\n\n**Expanding State Structure**\n\nI\'ve significantly expanded the state structure in `/src/store/useAppStore.ts`. Now, I\'m incorporating state variables for numerous aspects. Global clauses are stored in `globalClauses`, audit logs in `auditLogs`, and generated documents in `generatedDocuments`.  Added specific variables for HITL (Human-in-the-Loop) review, including `hitlTokens` and `hitlOriginalText`. Also included `formValues`, `isAnalyzing`, and methods like `startHitlReview`.\n\n\n"
