  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Request:** \"ponme en el perfil de un abogado con los permisos de abogado\" (Set the current user profile to \'Abogado\' with appropriate permissions).\n  - **Status:** COMPLETED (Implementation of the profile system and modal is finished; integration into the UI is the next logical step).\n\n2. User Knowledge\n- **User Identity:** stephaniamontero84@gmail.com\n- **Preferences:** The user is working within the Dominican Republic legal jurisdiction.\n- **Context:** The user requested to operate under a specific role (\"Abogado\") to test/utilize associated permissions.\n- **Scope:** The system now supports role-based access control (RBAC) via `UserRole` (\'ABOGADO\', \'NOTARIO\', \'ASISTENTE_LEGAL\', \'ADMIN\') and a `UserPermissions` matrix.\n\n3. Work Accomplished\n- **User Profile System:**\n  - Defined `UserProfile`, `UserRole`, and `UserPermissions` interfaces in `/src/types.ts`.\n  - Created `/src/core/userProfiles.ts` containing the permission matrix (`ROLE_PERMISSIONS`) and default profiles (`AVAILABLE_PROFILES`).\n  - Updated `src/store/useAppStore.ts` to include `currentUser` in the global state, added `switchUserRole` and `updateUserProfile` methods, and exposed `currentUser` and `permissions` to the application.\n  - Integrated `currentUser` data into `recordAudit` (for audit logs) and `createTemplate` (for author attribution).\n- **UI Components:**\n  - Created `/src/components/UserProfileModal.tsx` which allows viewing current credentials, switching roles, and editing user profile details.\n- **System Integration:**\n  - Updated `saveGeneratedDocument` to automatically attribute documents to the current user.\n\n4. Model Knowledge\n- **Architecture:**\n  - State management is centralized in `/src/store/useAppStore.ts` using a `globalState` pattern with `localStorage` persistence (`save_legal_platform_v2_state`).\n  - The `recordAudit` function is the central point for logging actions, now enriched with `currentUser` details.\n- **Permissions:**\n  - Permissions are strictly defined in `ROLE_PERMISSIONS` within `/src/core/userProfiles.ts`.\n  - The UI (once integrated) should check `permissions` from the store to conditionally render buttons (e.g., delete, publish).\n- **Constraints:**\n  - The current implementation of `useAppStore` initializes with `LAWYER_DEFAULT_PROFILE` if no state is found in `localStorage`.\n\n5. Files and Code\n- **Edited Files:**\n  - `/src/types.ts`: Added `UserRole`, `UserPermissions`, and `UserProfile` interfaces.\n  - `/src/store/useAppStore.ts`: Added `currentUser` state, `switchUserRole`, `updateUserProfile`, and updated `recordAudit` and `createTemplate` to use user context.\n- **Created Files:**\n  - `/src/core/userProfiles.ts`: Defines roles, permissions, and default profiles.\n  - `/src/components/UserProfileModal.tsx`: Modal component for user profile management.\n- **Viewed Files:**\n  - `/src/components/Navbar.tsx`: Relevant for integrating the `UserProfileModal` trigger.\n  - `/src/components/TemplateList.tsx`: Relevant for potential permission-based UI restrictions.\n\n6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Current Status:** The infrastructure for user roles and profiles is fully implemented.\n- **Next Steps:**\n  - Integrate the `UserProfileModal` into the `Navbar` (e.g., add a user avatar button in the top right).\n  - Implement permission checks in the UI (e.g., disable \"Delete\" or \"Publish\" buttons if `permissions.canDeleteTemplates` or `permissions.canPublishTemplates` is false).\n- **Directives:** The user\'s last request was to be put into the lawyer profile. The code is ready; the next agent should focus on the UI integration in `/src/components/Navbar.tsx`."
