  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Requirement**\n\nI\'m deep in thought, dissecting the user\'s request. My focus now is on eliminating horizontal scroll across the application while incorporating vertical scroll within the split view. This is driven by the need to contain overflowing text within a white box, but also permit page preview functionality. I\'m carefully considering how to implement this without sacrificing the user\'s ability to preview the text across pages.\n\n\n**Refining the Split View**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the split view\'s responsiveness, particularly regarding the text preview. I\'m prioritizing clean vertical scrolling with `overflow-y-auto overflow-x-hidden`, and ensuring text wraps properly within the defined container. Additionally, I\'m working on paginated visual page breaks for a realistic document preview, considering various page sizes and adding headers and footers. The goal is a truly responsive UI that adapts elegantly to different screen sizes, possibly stacking components on smaller devices.\n\n\n**Implementing New UI**\n\nI\'m now focused on enhancing the template editor in `DocumentEditor.tsx`. My current task is to implement a new \"Modo Formulario Estructurado (Estilo Google Forms)\" view alongside the existing editor. This new mode will offer intuitive, section-based form editing for lawyers and other users. I intend to retain the current raw text editor as a toggleable option.\n\n\n"
