    thinking: "**Analyzing Document Editor**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `DocumentEditor.tsx`. I need to remove the horizontal scroll and add a vertical one in the split view because the text overflows the white box. Also, I must ensure that the text can be previewed with page breaks.\n\n\n**Investigating Overflow Issues**\n\nI\'ve been digging into the `DocumentEditor.tsx` file and identified the root cause of the horizontal scroll and text overflow. It boils down to how the split view handles width constraints, especially on narrower screens. Specifically, the `w-1/2` class in conjunction with other width and overflow settings was the main culprit, along with the white paper preview having problems too. I\'m focusing on the `break-words` and realistic page breaks now.\n\n\n**Designing Page Breaks and Views**\n\nI\'m now implementing the paginated view, with clear page breaks, headers, and page numbers, allowing the text to flow across discrete physical pages with a toggle between \"Paginated View\" and \"Continuous View\". The paginated view will feature clean vertical scrolling and no horizontal scroll, using the `overflow-y-auto overflow-x-hidden` classes.\n\\n\\n\n\n\n"
