  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Eliminating Horizontal Scrolling**\n\nI\'ve started by addressing the pervasive horizontal scroll issue. My initial step involves a global CSS rule in `src/index.css` applied to the `html` element. This should provide a baseline for eliminating the problem across all screens and views.\n\n\n**Implementing Page Breaks**\n\nI\'m now focused on generating realistic page breaks within the legal documents. I\'m building a reusable `<PaginatedDocumentPreview>` component. It will intelligently split the contract text into pages, either using character/line density or explicit delimiters. The aim is to create visual \"Notarial Sheets\" with a white paper look.\n\n\n**Designing Notarial Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial notarial document elements. I\'m focusing on features such as 2.5cm borders, a header/jurisdiction section (\"REP\303\232BLICA DOMINICANA \342\200\224 ACTO AUT\303\211NTICO / CONTRATO PRIVADO\"), and a footer with \"P\303\241gina 1 de 3\" numbering. There\'s also a signature line at the end. I\'m ensuring support for view toggles: \"Vista Paginada (Hojas Notariales),\" \"Vista Continua,\" and \"Modo Impresi\303\263n,\" plus zoom controls.\n\nI\'m working on an intuitive, Google Forms-style template editor in `GoogleFormsTemplateEditor.tsx`, as requested. It introduces a mode switcher within `DocumentEditor.tsx`. Users will be able to select between a structured Google Forms style and a more advanced text/WordprocessingML editor.\n\n\n**Defining Template Sections**\n\nI\'m now detailing the structure of the Google Forms-style template editor. Visual sections will have colored header borders, titles, and descriptions, much like Google Forms. I\'m focusing on \"Question / Field Cards\" within these sections. These cards will feature a title, field type selector with icons, and a tag identifier badge. I\'m planning to use snake_case for the badge ID.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 757118015
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
