  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Envisioning Vertical Scroll**\n\nI\'m focusing intently on the notarial preview\'s vertical scrolling. My goal is to craft a seamlessly styled experience. No clipping, no locking; just fluid, smooth scrolling for effortless multi-page document navigation.\n\n\n**Implementing Full Permissions**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to user permissions, updating all roles to have unrestricted feature access. This means `ABOGADO`, `NOTARIO`, `ASISTENTE_LEGAL`, and `ADMIN` will have full permissions. Next, I\'ll be designing a comprehensive Office/Word-style Legal Ribbon Toolbar to make navigation easier. I plan to add tabs for Archive, Home, and many other useful features.\n\n\n**Expanding Toolbar Functions**\n\nI\'m now expanding the toolbar\'s capabilities. I\'m adding an \"Insertar\" tab with options for pages, tables (various sizes plus custom), illustrations (stamps, seals, signatures, QR codes), headers and footers (notarial letterhead, page numbers, jurisdiction info), text elements (text boxes, symbols, dates, JCE/RNC), links (bookmarks, linked clauses), and more.\n\n\n**Adding Advanced Notarial Tools**\n\nI\'m now integrating sophisticated notarial tools. This involves incorporating features for managing page layout (A4, 1-2 columns, paragraph spacing, organization), and adding references like table of contents, legal citations (Dominican laws and codes), and a table of legal authorities. I\'m also including mail merge capabilities, a step-by-step assistant for data input, and preview options.\n\n\n"
