  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Scrollbar Focus**\n\nOkay, I\'m zeroing in on the vertical scroll in the notarial preview. The explicit requirement is a scrollable container with a custom, styled vertical scrollbar. I\'m thinking of focusing on `overflow-y-auto overflow-x-hidden` for the implementation and aiming for a high-contrast page design. This seems like a good starting point.\n\n\n**Defining Office-Style Ribbon**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into replicating the Office/Word-style ribbon. I\'ve broken down the requested features, starting with the \"Archivo\" (Backstage) options: new document/template, open, save, print (PDF/dialog), share (notarial review link, clipboard copy), and export (DOCX, PDF, JSON, TXT). I\'m also planning the application options, user account, and document metadata. Then, I\'ll tackle the \"Inicio\" tab\'s clipboard and font formatting controls.\n\n\n**Expanding Paragraph Styling**\n\nI\'m now deep in paragraph formatting. I\'m focusing on text alignment and spacing, including specific presets like \"Notarial 1.15.\" Bullet points and numbering variations are next. I\'m also considering indentation and borders, plus custom styles. The styles are focused on common notarial document elements and now I\'m starting on the \"Insertar\" tab\'s elements.\n\n\n**Adding Inserted Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial \"Insertar\" tab elements. I\'m focusing on legal text boxes, notarial symbols, and solemn Dominican date/time stamps. I\'m also including options for JCE/RNC ID fields, along with hyperlinks and cross-references. I\'ll include legal review comment features, too.\n\n\n**Refining Page Layout**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in page layout. I\'m focusing on headers/footers, watermarks (\"ICO,\" \"CONFIDENCIAL,\" custom texts), and page borders (simple, double notarial, filigree). I\'m also configuring margins (Standard Notarial, Narrow, Wide), orientation, and paper sizes (Letter, Legal, A4). Paragraph spacing and first-line indentation are key. I\'ll get to tables of content, footnotes, legal citations, and legal authorities next.\n\n\n**Developing Correspondence Merge**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in correspondence merge capabilities, focusing on legal document generation. I am designing templates for notarial contracts, letters of intent, and legal notifications, including the creation of a mail merge assistant. I\'m focusing on the implementation of dynamic field insertion and preview. I\'ll soon tackle generating and exporting merged documents in both DOCX and PDF formats.\n\n\n**Implementing Review Functions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the \"Review\" functions. I\'ve got suggested changes, accepting/rejecting revisions. I\'ll include document protection, blocking editing and mandatory clause protection. Next, I\'ll incorporate the \"View\" features like notarial print design, continuous view, full-screen reading mode, and clause outline. Showing/hiding options are next, like ruler and notarial grid. I\'m also planning the zoom levels and windowing features. Finally, macros/scripts for repetitive clause generation are next.\n\n\n**Structuring Ribbon Architecture**\n\nI\'m now structuring the ribbon architecture, aiming for modularity. I\'m building a suite of components for the Legal Ribbon and Notarial Studio to maintain clean, maintainable, and responsive code. I\'m focusing on the component structure, starting with the main `LegalRibbon.tsx` and a `BackstageModal.tsx`. Next, I\'ll tackle contextual tabs for clicked elements.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 440952831
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
