  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Notarial Ribbon**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into designing the Notarial Ribbon. My current focus is figuring out what features will be in each tab to design the UI/UX. The first tab is Archive, or Backstage. I\'m taking the full ribbon into consideration, including contextual tabs. This requires considering each of the 11 main tabs.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Backstage Features**\n\nNow, I\'m analyzing the features for the Backstage. I\'ve broken it down into sections. Info will include metadata and validation. \"Nuevo\" allows for blank docs or templates. \"Abrir\" opens templates, and \"Guardar\" keeps changes. \"Compartir\" offers a notarial link, and \"Exportar\" covers document formats. I\'m focusing on \"Opciones y Configuraci\303\263n\" next, considering jurisdictional profiles. Then, I\'ll review \"Cuenta.\"\n\n\n**Defining Text Formatting Options**\n\nI\'m now defining text formatting options. This includes text size, bold, italics, underline, strikethrough, text color choices (Notarial Black, Legal Navy, Burgundy, Graphite), highlighting (Yellow, Green, Cyan, Pink), and case formatting.\n\nI\'m also considering paragraph formatting with alignment, line spacing options (Simple, Notarial, 1.5, Double), bulleted and numbered lists (Notarial formats included), indentation controls, and paragraph borders/shading. I\'ve begun defining styles such as \"Normal,\" \"Notarial Act Title,\" \"Chapter/Section,\" \"Solemn Clause,\" \"Legal Citation,\" and \"Appearance.\" I\'m also planning interactive \"Find and Replace\" functionality.\n\nI\'m now moving on to the \"Insert\" tab, and planning to define available options for pages, tables, and illustrations.\n\n\n**Expanding the \"Insert\" Tab**\n\nI\'m expanding the \"Insert\" tab options. This now includes elements like digital verification QR codes and digitized notarial signatures. I\'m also planning headers and footers with notarial branding. Text options will encompass legal text boxes and notarial symbols, along with date/time formatting. I\'ve added fields for Dominican ID numbers. Plus, links and comments are in.\n\nI\'m now detailing design and page layout features.\n\n\n**Defining the \"Combinar\" Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into the \"Combinar\" features. I\'m focusing on \"Datos combinados\" to add source fields, and the \"Vista previa de resultados combinados\" to toggle real values versus tags. Ultimately, I\'ll allow users to combine, print, and download in batch DOCX/PDF formats.\n\nI\'m moving on to the contextual tabs now.\n\n\n**Refining Contextual Tab Features**\n\nI\'m currently refining the contextual tab features, specifically focusing on how they appear when a component like a seal, table, or header is selected. For seal/signature formatting, I\'m considering size, opacity, position, notarial title, and authentication code. Table design includes notarial table styles, and options for managing rows and columns. Header/footer design covers the letterhead, page number placement, and header margins. Moreover, I\'m integrating vertical scroll features into the notarial preview. I\'m focusing on implementation with custom scrollbars and page navigation.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 616053568
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
