  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Fetch Failures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on where the `window.fetch` setter is failing. It seems that in browser environments, particularly within secure iframes like those in AI Studio\'s preview, `window.fetch` might only have a getter. There are also indications that scripts could be attempting to set `window.fetch` or assign `fetch` directly, potentially causing the issue. Hold on.\n\n\n**Analyzing Fetch Protection**\n\nI\'m now investigating JavaScript property definitions and how they relate to the `window.fetch` issue. It seems a script could define `window.fetch` using `Object.defineProperty` with only a getter, leading to the error when a setter is attempted. I think I\'ll try defining a getter and setter on `window` early in `index.html` or `main.tsx` to safeguard `window.fetch`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 748106516
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
