  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Contract Storage**\n\nI\'m currently focused on pinpointing the ideal name and implementation details for the requested \"final contracts\" section. The user\'s need for a distinct, easily accessible location is clear: it must be a prominent section for storing and retrieving completed, non-template contracts.\n\n\n**Expanding Contract Storage**\n\nI\'ve been exploring naming conventions, and \"Contratos Finales,\" \"B\303\263veda de Contratos Finales,\" and \"Contratos Emitidos\" are leading contenders. I\'m enhancing `DocumentsVault.tsx` with initial sample contracts for immediate user experience. The enhancements include filter tabs (\"Todos los Contratos Finales,\" etc.), detailed contract cards with status badges and actions, a \"+ Redactar Nuevo Contrato Final\" button, and quick search functionality. My goal is a robust, user-friendly storage solution.\n\n\n**Designing Sidebar Navigation**\n\nI\'m now integrating filtering by contract title, party names (like \"Juan P\303\251rez\"), and IDs (c\303\251dula, RNC). A total statistics bar reflecting contracts (Total, Notarized, Pending) is being considered. The user prefers a lateral menu. I\'m building a `Sidebar.tsx` component, replacing the top bar, with a clear brand section (logo, platform name, version, and flag) and a primary \"Generate Final Contract\" action. The sidebar will have a \"FINAL CONTRACTS\" navigation section.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 177746975
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
