    thinking: "**Envisioning a Richer Interface**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on significantly improving `DocumentsVault.tsx`. My focus is on transforming it into a \"B\303\263veda de Contratos Finales\" \342\200\223 a central repository for issued and notarized contracts. I\'ve started thinking through key enhancements. Right now, I\'m prioritizing the title and header to be more descriptive and user-friendly, envisioning \"Contratos Finales & Actos Notariados Emitidos.\" The goal is clarity.\n\n\n**Expanding the Document View**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the document viewer itself. I\'m conceptualizing togglable view modes, which should allow the user to see things differently. I have ideas for three key viewing modes: \"Vista Impresi\303\263n Notarial Formal,\" \"Texto Legal Editable,\" and \"Variables Capturadas.\" Also, I\'m thinking of enabling in-place editing for the final contract text, and that the \"Vista Impresi\303\263n Notarial Formal\" should have a watermark, margins, and notary stamp.\n\n\n**Designing Action Buttons**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out the action buttons for each contract. I\'m focusing on key features like downloading as Word documents, printing or generating PDFs, duplication, in-place editing, status changes, and deletion. I\'m also planning a modal that offers template selection when a user initiates a new contract.\n\\n\\n\n**Building the Sidebar Component**\n\nI\'m now deep in the design of the sidebar, `src/components/Sidebar.tsx`. I\'m going for a sleek, dark, high-contrast look, using a modern legal color scheme. The header will feature a scalable shield icon, \"SAVE Legal\", a subtitle, and the version. A prominent CTA for \"+ Generar Contrato Final\" will be included, alongside navigation groups for Contracts & Documents, specifically \"Contratos Finales (B\303\263veda)\".\n\n\n"
