  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the UI Design**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on dissecting the SAVE Pricing & Checkout UI. Specifically, I\'m breaking down the top navigation bar. I\'ve noted the \'S\' monogram on the left, next to the word SAVE, as well as the \'Templates\' and \'Pricing\' labels. I am breaking it down component by component to determine if the images provided help determine an accurate determination. I am using the components described to determine the efficacy of the provided images.\n\n\n**Evaluating the Navigation Elements**\n\nI\'ve moved on from the navigation bar and am now examining the pricing section of the UI. I\'m focusing on the \"How it works\" section, Login, and Get Started buttons. The hero title uses a serif font, elegant Libre Caslon, and the subtitle has Plus Jakarta Sans. The three pricing cards are next; the \"Single Template\" and \"Professional\" cards\' design elements are key. I\'m paying attention to the description, features, and call-to-action buttons in each card to understand how the plans are designed.\n\n\n**Dissecting Pricing Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the pricing card details. Specifically, I see a \"Most Popular\" gold badge on the Professional plan. The white \"Professional\" title contrasts with the gold badge and larger white price text. The feature list with gold checkmarks reinforces the benefits. The CTA button for the Professional card is a warm golden color with dark text. The \"Enterprise\" plan is labeled Custom, with a tailored description. I\'m noting the differences and how the features are presented.\n\n\n\n**Reviewing Checkout Components**\n\nI\'m now examining the checkout form and order summary, starting with payment details. I\'m noting the VISA/MC badges and the required fields: card number, expiry, CVC, and name on card. A security notice regarding encryption is present. The \"Pay\" button\'s design is dark green with white text and an arrow, a strong call-to-action. On the right, the order summary details the document item and the subtotal, tax, and total. Trust badges are shown. Finally, I\'m noting the footer elements.\n\n\n**Defining the Design Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the SAVE design system, specifically its color palette, typography, and button styles. I\'ve broken down the color tokens, noting the primary deep forest green, secondary warm cream, and tertiary ochre gold, along with their respective scales. I\'ve also identified Libre Caslon Text for headlines and Plus Jakarta Sans for body and label text. I am also identifying and classifying the primary, secondary, inverted, outlined, and tertiary buttons, making notes on their key properties.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 590367739
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
